{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551275-bone-flowers-ch\u2019ing-shih-flaw","id":1551275,"title":"Bone Flowers Ch\u2019ing Shih flaw","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-05-25T14:56:37-07:00","id":1551275,"title":"Bone Flowers Ch\u2019ing Shih flaw","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> Putting this question here as it is vampire adjacent, using the Kuei-jin.<br /> <br /> The Bone Flowers Dharma book has the Ch\u2019ing Shih flaw. What is the exactly the flaw meant to be disadvanteous at? Being Appareance 0? Or being imbalanced?<br /> <br /> I assumed that it was Appareance 0, but the text of the flaw makes it sound like it is just a progressive state (as per Yin Imbalance in the KoTE Core book).<br /> <br /> So, what is the actually disadvantage that the Flaw imposses?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-25T16:03:04-07:00","id":1551279,"title":"","content":"(Dry heaves at 90s WW's inability to handle aspirant marks in Romanization)<br /> <br /> It might be for when characters that aren't usually Yin Imbalanced suffer from being a chiang-shih* because you got a flaw, but it's more likely to have been intended to cover the onerous mechanics of decaying to Appearance 0 as something that grants freebies in chargen. As in, when you take the flaw, you opt to speedrun the process of Yin Imbalance instead of letting it happen in play. It can also act as a cover designation for canon characters with Yin Imbalance, rather than just setting the character's Appearance to 0 and assuming that people will know a Yin Imbalanced character with a portrait that looks like it rivals a Nosferatu is a chiang-shih, as in the mechanical term.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">*This is actually how you render jiangshi in Wade-Giles, sans tones.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-25T17:24:35-07:00","id":1551280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551275-bone-flowers-ch\u2019ing-shih-flaw?p=1551279#post1551279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Dry heaves at 90s WW's inability to handle aspirant marks in Romanization)<br /> <br /> It might be for when characters that aren't usually Yin Imbalanced suffer from being a chiang-shih* because you got a flaw, but it's more likely to have been intended to cover the onerous mechanics of decaying to Appearance 0 as something that grants freebies in chargen. As in, when you take the flaw, you opt to speedrun the process of Yin Imbalance instead of letting it happen in play. It can also act as a cover designation for canon characters with Yin Imbalance, rather than just setting the character's Appearance to 0 and assuming that people will know a Yin Imbalanced character with a portrait that looks like it rivals a Nosferatu is a chiang-shih, as in the mechanical term.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">*This is actually how you render jiangshi in Wade-Giles, sans tones.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>So if I am getting this right. I made Yue a Bone Flower character, I take the flaw, I get Appearance 0 as my mechanical effect?<br /> <br /> Or could I have a Yin 5, Yang 1 starting character (Yin imbalance), with Appareance 5 take this flaw and what would it be during the game?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-25T23:12:44-07:00","id":1551286,"title":"","content":"Personally I interpreted it like the Cappadocian Clan Flaw with an added extra<br /> <br /> You take the Flaw you will have a Yin Immbalance from the start and Appearance 0 (regardless of your stats, but obviously your Chi reserves will mirror your imbalance) - with all of its mechanical negativity and like how the text say some Courts outright despise you like the Golden Court (or any Court really) where Yang is faroved, to look &quot;Human&quot; and the corpse like hideuos death visage is something that is frowned uppon (hid behind a fan and whispers).<br /> Also the potential confusion you are a Running Monkey yet people potentially think you are an old and enlightened Bone Flower and bring a tons of headache<br /> Aside those you either use the text-mentioned ritual to look your idealised self, but still a corpse or to &quot;repair&quot; your Appearance 0/Chi imbalance, get a Bodishatva with Equilibrium to help you &quot;back&quot; <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-26T01:57:09-07:00","id":1551290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551275-bone-flowers-ch\u2019ing-shih-flaw?p=1551280#post1551280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So if I am getting this right. I made Yue a Bone Flower character, I take the flaw, I get Appearance 0 as my mechanical effect?<br /> <br /> Or could I have a Yin 5, Yang 1 starting character (Yin imbalance), with Appareance 5 take this flaw and what would it be during the game?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think the strongest intended purpose is for a character with a Yin Imbalance to start out with Appearance 0 at chargen getting 3 extra freebies for being able to blend in with the Nosferatu. It's also possible that you don't need to have a Yin Imbalance and just had a really unlucky bout of being Imbalanced (and decaying down to Appearance 0) before correcting course, but that seems a bit overly complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-26T08:07:30-07:00","id":1551295,"title":"","content":"I don't have access to my KotE books. From what I remember it's possible for a character who is heavily Yin chi imbalanced (to the point that their appearance has become zero) to slowly rebalance their chi and restore their appearance. This flaw makes the 0 appearance permanent, so even if they end up becoming permanently Yang imbalanced, they're still going to have the zero appearance. If you're planning to go heavily yin chi imbalance anyway, then you're going to get a 0 appearance and this flaw is basically just some freebie points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T17:37:08-08:00","id":1557287,"title":"","content":"Thread Necromancy, but it became relevant to the game we are finally, FINALLY starting.<br /> <br /> <br /> Can you combine this flaw with Monstrous, or is it too powergaming? I was thinking of comments made by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> and we had a discussion, my friend wants to combine both flaws, I am of the opinion that it is getting 6 freebies for the same effect (Appearance 0) is too much, especially when Appearance has always been the dump stat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-18-2026, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-05T18:21:44-08:00","id":1557323,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's basically the same effect. <br /> <br /> If you did allow it to stack the character would go beyond simply being an undead corpse to the point of looking like some sort of freakish monstrosity, and even within Wan Kuei society many would assume that the character has been corrupted by the Yama Kings and react accordingly (ie look to kill the character). The character would likely have to largely exist outside of the Court system and that would simply cause too many conflicts and problems with the overall chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-07T07:08:08-08:00","id":1557365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551275-bone-flowers-ch\u2019ing-shih-flaw?p=1557323#post1557323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's basically the same effect.<br /> <br /> If you did allow it to stack the character would go beyond simply being an undead corpse to the point of looking like some sort of freakish monstrosity, and even within Wan Kuei society many would assume that the character has been corrupted by the Yama Kings and react accordingly (ie look to kill the character). The character would likely have to largely exist outside of the Court system and that would simply cause too many conflicts and problems with the overall chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a mixed splat group: a Kitsune (our social specialist), an Orphan mage (myself, mental specialist) a Stargazer Ahroun (muscle), and a Song of the Shadow Kuei Jin (my friend, our all-rounder), so being outside the Courts could give us plot points, but not initially relevant. We would, though, lose the whole other social network that a Court could provide.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> We have optimizing our stats for our roles and to minimise our future XP expenditure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-07-2026, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}